{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.six_term_mass_formula_complete","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.six_term_mass_formula_complete","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.six_term_mass_formula_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.six_term_mass_formula_complete","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/six_term_mass_formula_complete.lean#L104-L117","doc":"**Six-term unified mass formula** ([`prop:six-term-mass-formula-complete`]).\n\nThe claim of the block, as a proposition over caller-supplied data — **named,\nnot asserted**.\n\nRead the module docstring before using it: with `t₁ … t₆` opaque this states\nonly that `m` is their sum, and the six terms the `.md` names (`|tr_M(T_w)|`,\n`Σ Φ_q(|V̂_i|)`, …) are **not encoded anywhere in this file**. A caller who has\nactually constructed the six terms supplies them here; what they get is the\nadditive bookkeeping, not the manuscript's derivation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:six-term-mass-formula-complete","label":"thm:six-term-mass-formula-complete","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/six-term-mass-formula-complete.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_sixTermSplit_of_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_sixTermSplit_of_independent","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/six_term_mass_formula_complete.lean#L94-L102","doc":"**And it does constrain the mass.** Chosen independently of the terms, the\nsplit fails — so the schema pins `m` to the sum and says nothing else.\n\nRecorded as a theorem because it is also the reason a `sorry` would be the\nwrong disposition here: it would read as \"true, not yet proved\" over a\nstatement refutable at free data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sixTermSplit_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sixTermSplit_sum","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/six_term_mass_formula_complete.lean#L88-L92","doc":"**The schema constrains nothing about the terms.** For *any* six elements\nthere is a mass satisfying the split — namely their sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sixTermSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sixTermSplit","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/six_term_mass_formula_complete.lean#L77-L86","doc":"**A six-way additive split**: `m = t₁ + t₂ + t₃ + t₄ + t₅ + t₆`.\n\nThis is the *shape* of the manuscript's six-term formula with all six terms\nleft opaque. It is named here so the distance between the shape and the claim\nis visible in the Lean rather than only in prose. See\n`sixTermSplit_sum` and `not_sixTermSplit_of_independent` for exactly how much\nit constrains. ","signatureChunk":0}]}